---
import "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/brand.css";
import "../../../../packages/ui/src/glass/glass.css";
import "../installer.css";

import Footer from "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/Header.astro";
import ThemeInit from '../../../../packages/ui/src/brand/ThemeInit.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><ThemeInit external />
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Permissions & privacy · SAM installer</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/sam-head.png" />
    <link
      rel="preload"
      href="/fonts/Chillax-Variable.woff2"
      as="font"
      type="font/woff2"
      crossorigin
    />
    
    
    
  </head>
  <body class="sam-form">
    <Header compact icon="/brand-icon.png" />
    <main class="privacy-main">

      <span class="badge">Your access. Your choice.</span>
      <h1>Permissions<br />& <span class="gradient-text">privacy.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro">Know what you’re sharing, what we create, and what stays yours.</p>
<p>No GitHub account is needed to get SAM running in Cloudflare. Signing in afterwards requires GitHub, GitLab or Google; there is no email login.</p>
      <div class="privacy-content sam-glass sam-glass-rim">
        <h2>What you authorize</h2>
        <p>
          Default bootstrap mode requests account read access and permission to deploy Workers.
          Cloudflare’s permissions may cover existing Workers in the selected account. Only approve
          accounts you intend to use. Experimental full installation requires broader resource and
          token-provisioning permissions; it is not enabled or verified for general use.
        </p>
        <h2>Temporary access</h2>
        <p>
          The installer handles OAuth tokens server-side in an isolated session. Hosted access
          expires after 15 minutes by default, bounded by token expiry. In this preview branch,
          handoff removes hosted OAuth and deployment-credential copies but retains a bounded claim
          record until the original expiry so interrupted handoff can be retried. Disconnect and
          expiry attempt cleanup and revocation; provider failures can delay deletion or revocation.
          Use Cloudflare’s authorized-applications screen to revoke access yourself if needed. No
          central refresh token is retained.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your password is entered only on Cloudflare. This app does not use analytics, third-party
          scripts, or application request logging. Hosting and network providers may still process
          request metadata.
        </p>
        <p>
          If cleanup is interrupted after a grant expires, this tab can keep a nonsecret cleanup
          reference. Reconnect with Cloudflare and choose “Finish cleanup” to remove unused setup
          credentials. The reference grants no access by itself; credentials already owned by your
          installation service are preserved.
        </p>
        <h2>What stays in your account</h2>
        <p>
          Default mode creates a maintenance Worker without an ongoing Cloudflare deployment token.
          This preview branch adds durable recovery: save the browser-generated credential before
          claiming ownership. Its hash stays in your account; maintenance sessions last 24 hours by
          default. Recovery login replaces the previous active session. Replacement credentials
          become active only after you save and confirm them. Earlier hosted revisions may still
          have temporary owner access; check the displayed source version.
        </p>
        <p>
          Experimental full mode temporarily handles installation credentials during bootstrap, then
          transfers deployment and storage authority to your maintenance service and narrower
          runtime authority to SAM. This lifecycle still needs live validation, including the effect
          of OAuth revocation on derived credentials. It is not a claim that credentials never reach
          our service. Disconnecting does not delete transferred resources. Review resource
          identities and backups before removing a test installation; automatic uninstall is not
          provided.
        </p>
        <p>
          Experimental full-mode builders preserve approved SAM source and Git history, build
          artifacts and deployment checkpoints in your account's R2 storage. Saved source is
          verified against its commit, tree and content digest before reuse. Toolchain and
          dependency downloads can still require network access. The approved code and its build
          dependencies are trusted deployment code running with your installation's authority;
          nested build containers are not a security boundary against malicious build scripts.
        </p>
        <h2>Your choice</h2>
        <p>
          You can deploy this same installer yourself and register your own OAuth client. Source
          availability helps you review the app; it does not guarantee that a hosted operator cannot
          modify its deployment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer compact icon="/sam-head.png"><a href="/privacy.html">Permissions & privacy</a><a href="/self-host.html">Self-host</a><span id="version"></span></Footer>
  </body>
</html>
